finding.evidence:
GET /api/BasketItems with Authorization: Bearer <customer i35test JWT (UserId 31, BasketId 11)> -> 200 1045 bytes
{"status":"success","data":[{"ProductId":1,"BasketId":1,"id":1,...},{"ProductId":4,"BasketId":2,"id":4,...},{"ProductId":4,"BasketId":3,"id":5,...},{"ProductId":4,"BasketId":4,"id":6,...},...]}
The returned BasketIds (1,2,3,4...) do not belong to the caller's basket (11), proving the collection query has no ownership filter. Basket 1 is owned by UserId 1 per the /rest/basket/1 response.

GET /api/Complaints with Authorization: Bearer <customer i35test JWT (UserId 31)> -> 200 219 bytes
{"status":"success","data":[{"UserId":3,"id":1,"message":"I'll build my own eCommerce business! With Black Jack! And Hookers!","file":null,...}]}
The only returned complaint belongs to UserId 3, not the caller (31), showing no owner/role restriction.
